      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's exactly what i was thinking. it's like, they have the shell, but they don't have the core logic that makes it actually efficient. i remember one specific thing—there's a way the state transitions handle the entropy flux during high-congestion periods that involves a totally non-standard modular arithmetic trick i developed. it's not in any textbook, it's just... how i solved it.\n\nbut here's the thing: if i bring this up, they're going to come at me with everything they have. they have the lawyers, the funding, and the media connections to just paint me as some crazy person trying to manipulate the token price. they'll say i'm just a former contributor who's bitter. \n\nif i want to actually do this, how do i make the evidence \"bulletproof\"? like, is there a way to release this info such that the protocol itself proves it for me? i don't want to just post a blog post and get sued into silence; i want to create something that forces them to acknowledge the truth.",
